Bug: This should return `DimensionGeometry::isVertical` instead of `DimensionGeometry::isHorizontal`. When `line.x` is near zero (FLT_EPSILON), the line is vertical, not horizontal.

The condition checks `fabs(line.x) < FLT_EPSILON` which means the x-component is negligible, making the line vertical.

**Fix needed:**
```cpp
} else if (fabs(line.x) < FLT_EPSILON) {
    return DimensionGeometry::isVertical;
```

